    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51053" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">virgĕus</span></b> , a, um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of rods</i> or <i>twigs</i>, <i>of
				brushwood</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scopae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 152</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">crates,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					1, 6, 22</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">saepes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					11, 3, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">anuli ex myrto,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					15, 29, 37, § 124</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">supellex,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 1, 165</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">flamma,</span>”
				<i>of brush set on fire</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. A.
					7, 463</span></i>
			.</div>
